# Text files are checked out with LF on every system, so a Windows clone
# (core.autocrlf=true by default, also on the CI runners) builds the same
# embedded shaders and test fixtures as macOS and Linux: CRLF changed the
# WGSL sources (and their recorded function checks), XMP and SQL fixtures.
# Rawtonic itself reads CRLF files from other programs (tested), it does not
# depend on this.
* text=auto eol=lf
